<title>AUSTRALIA: ANZ says needs to improve N.Z. operation.</title>
<headline>ANZ says needs to improve N.Z. operation.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-08-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australia and New Zealand Banking Group Ltd (ANZ) on Friday said it needed to make a major improvement in the efficiency of its New Zealand operation.</p>
<p>In documents presented to an analysts' briefing and released to the Australian Stock Exchange, the bank said other weaknesses it faced in New Zealand were a high cost structure, shrinking margins on interest income and a competitive market.</p>
<p>ANZ said its strengths in New Zealand included strong non-interest income, a high profile and a stable and diverse franchise.</p>
<p>-- Melbourne bureau 613-9286-1421</p>
</text>
